<title>NEW ZEALAND: Lion H1 profit falls to NZ$72.2 mln.</title>
<headline>Lion H1 profit falls to NZ$72.2 mln.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1996-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr result to Feb 28</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				  72.2 vs 91.2</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)				 13.2 vs 16.7</p>
<p>    Div (cents)				  8.0 vs same</p>
<p>    Turnover				   914.6 vs 937.8</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			    118.0 vs 134.5</p>
<p>    Tax					   46.8 vs 44.4</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)	 547.7 vs same</p>
<p>Dividend carries no imputation credit.  </p>
<p>Note - Lion Nathan Ltd is an Australasian brewing and beverage company. Market expectations were for a net profit of NZ$65-70 million.</p>
</text>
